course: dictionary
lesson: 11544
title: Amelioration: making things better
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are long and formal. You meet them in history books, science reports and exam texts. Amelioration is one of these words, but you can work out its meaning from the clues around it, and it even sounds a little like «better».
explain: «The council worked hard on the amelioration of living conditions in the old streets.» The clues are worked hard and old streets, which suggests the streets were in a poor state. Living conditions are how people live, so amelioration must mean making things better. Try the swap: «the council worked hard on making living conditions better». It still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: «Farmers noticed the amelioration of the soil after they added compost.» The soil had been poor, and compost helped it. Amelioration is a noun for the process of getting better, so you say «the amelioration», not «an amelioration».
fact: Amelioration means making something bad better, or the process of it getting better.
fact: It is a formal word, found in serious writing such as history, science and exams.
fact: It is uncountable, so we say «the amelioration of the soil», not «an amelioration».
fact: The word sounds a little like «better», and the sentence around it often shows what was bad before.
fact: A good check is to swap in «making something better» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The council worked hard on the amelioration of living conditions.» What does amelioration mean here? | Moving people to a new town | *Making living conditions better | Counting the people who live there | Making living conditions worse
exercise: The school made its damaged playground safer and nicer. Which word describes this change? | Barely | Ancient | Curt | *Amelioration
exercise: Is amelioration something you can count, like one amelioration and two ameliorations? | No, because it is a verb | Yes, but only in history books | Yes, you can say two ameliorations | *No, it is uncountable, so we say the amelioration
test: «Scientists studied the amelioration of the river after the factory closed.» What does amelioration mean? | Moving to a new place | Getting dirtier and more polluted | *Getting cleaner and healthier | Drying up completely
test: Mum says, «The amelioration of our roof will cost a lot.» Which phrase could replace amelioration without changing the meaning? | Breaking the roof | *Making the roof better | Making the roof louder | Painting the roof red
exam: Which meaning is the opposite of amelioration? | *Making something worse | Making a new plan | Making something better | Improving the soil
